      "mergedPostDetails": "1.) Start the game with a \"normal\", known good avatar.\n\n2) Switch to a non humanoid avatar and back to a known good one.\n\n3) Observe that your mirror reflection is now frozen.\n\nWhen switching avatars, you will see yourself moving in the mirror for a few frames, and then freeze again\n\nALSO\n\nThe mesh of the previous model stays in the scene. Sometimes it remains textured, and sometimes it just turns magenta (missing texture).\n\nI cannot get rid of this (switching avatars and worlds) until I completely restart the client. I will always drag the corpes of the one \"bad\" avatar with me - local only (this does not sync over).\n\nCurrently I'm unable to provide logs, since this build does create log files, but does not write to them at all. (they are empty)",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1351] Avatars freeze in mirror after using non humanoid avatar",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "651eab33fb436dc993bc161b",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello!  Thanks for reporting this.  \n\nIs this still happening for you?\n\nIf so, can you provide avatars you can successfully repro with?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
